bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    jit_unsafe_optional_as_cast_garbage_2026_11_09, 0, "2026-11-10 fix: MIR lower_cast_expr (lowering_expr_ops.rs) emitted a plain MirInst::Cast on the boxed Option carrier for T?/Option<T> sources, bit-copying the heap word. Fix: for a numeric target whose source is a registry optional or Option enum, call rt_unwrap_or_trap (None traps like unwrap), decode the payload to its native payload type via unbox_scalar_for_raw_slot, then Cast payload_ty -> target. Repro+prevention: src/compiler_rust/compiler/tests/compile_and_run.rs unsafe_optional_u64_as_cast_extracts_payload, unsafe_optional_i64_*, unsafe_optional_text_*, unsafe_option_enum_i64_*, unsafe_optional_as_cast_to_wider_int_*; red 0/5 passed (all returned 7) -> green 5/5. None case = checked abort via rt_unwrap_or_trap (not in-process testable)."
